{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "That's Christmas To Me and A Pentatonix Christmas combine the Christmas music I have repeatedly chosen with the vocal harmonies I want now.",
    "Those two albums feel like natural follow-ups because they connect my holiday listening with my interest in The New Old Fashioned."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Show tunes and operatic pop do not satisfy the same interest as Christmas vocal harmonies; having prominent singing is not enough for me.",
    "Country hits, a movie soundtrack, and a singer-songwriter album do not give me the holiday connection I want on this visit.",
    "Partners and Hope give me too little evidence of a close match to spend my limited listening time exploring them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The suggestions seem to treat an interest in vocal music as a reason to try many different singing styles, although the particular sound matters to me.",
    "My interest in The New Old Fashioned seems to have been stretched into an interest in older songs and broad hits collections."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated Christmas album choices are a stronger clue to what appeals to me here than a general interest in music with vocals.",
    "The combination of Christmas songs and vocal harmonies matters more to me than either connection by itself.",
    "I rarely explore unless something feels closely relevant, and even with two appealing Christmas albums I would only try one this visit."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The suggestions partly understood my interest in Christmas vocal harmonies but extended it too broadly to music that does not fit my current mood."
}"}
